WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.379
Use Flywheel inside your own ChatGPT or Claude account. This shows manual

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:08.253
setup before directory approval. Public

00:00:08.253 --> 00:00:10.980
comparisons need no Flywheel account.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:17.314
In Claude, open Customize, Connectors, Yours, then Add custom connector.

00:00:17.314 --> 00:00:23.560
Enter a name and paste the exact calculator server URL shown on screen.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:29.130
Choose Sign in when needed and Register automatically, then Add. In a

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:34.620
new chat, open the plus menu, choose Connectors and enable Flywheel.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:41.860
In ChatGPT, open Plugins, Add, then Add custom MCP server. Enter

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.028
the name and the same server

00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:49.440
URL. Choose OAuth or no authentication.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:59.825
Open Advanced OAuth settings. Use Dynamic Client Registration. Keep openid as the default scope and

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:10.420
offline_access as the base scope. Disable OIDC and clear its extra scopes. Create the private plugin.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:16.506
Choose Use without an account for public comparisons. For member features, sign in to

00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:22.520
Flywheel with your own account and emailed code. Never put that code in the AI chat.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:29.610
Check the Flywheel consent page and the return destination. Allow calculator access only if you

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:36.700
agree. It permits membership checks and calculations, not saved plans or GoMining transactions.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.738
Select Flywheel in your chat and ask what you want to compare. Confirm the miner kind and

00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:48.640
the planning date, not just the purchase date. Answer the relevant questions in stages.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:56.455
This confirmed fictional example compares maintenance for one ordinary miner. The actual result is about

00:01:56.455 --> 00:02:04.420
eighty cents without GOM payment and sixty-three cents with it. These are assumed costs, not a live quote.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:13.373
Compare loose GOM and locks, or BTC, GOM and TH reinvestment. Check all remaining assets and

00:02:13.373 --> 00:02:22.520
warnings. Unknown balances must stay unknown; the model does not rank whole-portfolio returns.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:29.814
A free Basic account does not unlock PLUS. Eligible PLUS and Founder accounts can use advanced

00:02:29.814 --> 00:02:34.159
calculations, within the connector limits. Disconnect in

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:37.340
your AI client to revoke that connection.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:44.676
The public maintenance example uses a fictional ordinary miner at one hundred terahash and

00:02:44.676 --> 00:02:51.849
twelve watts per terahash. The actual cost is point seven nine eight dollars without GOM

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:55.435
payment, or point six three dollars with it.

00:02:55.435 --> 00:03:00.000
Starting BTC is unknown; all remaining assets are shown.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:08.186
The thirty day GOM and locks comparison preserves one hundred terahash and point zero zero one five

00:03:08.186 --> 00:03:16.538
newly retained BTC in both cases. Baseline loose GOM ends at two hundred fifteen point two five, with

00:03:16.538 --> 00:03:20.920
two hundred fifty locked. The alternative has seventy

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.220
two point seven five loose, and four hundred locked.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:33.095
The reinvestment example shows four routes with different remaining assets. TH reinvestment ends

00:03:33.095 --> 00:03:40.725
near one hundred six point eight nine terahash, while the BTC route retains more BTC. This is

00:03:40.725 --> 00:03:48.600
not a whole portfolio ranking: miner resale values, taxes and unknown starting BTC are excluded.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:56.082
This is a presentation of the actual hosted OAuth replay, not an AI client screenshot. The dedicated PLUS

00:03:56.082 --> 00:04:02.994
account passed the advanced calculation with the exact fictional fixture. It allocated eighty six

00:04:02.994 --> 00:04:07.768
additional terahash initially. The result reports reserve shortfall

00:04:07.768 --> 00:04:11.260
days; that is not the same as unpaid maintenance.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:17.605
In the same real hosted PLUS replay, Horizons returned Ready. The TH system comparison

00:04:17.605 --> 00:04:23.951
exceeded the one point one hurdle. GOM also exceeded that numeric hurdle, but remained

00:04:23.951 --> 00:04:27.271
evidence gated. Its ending asset inventory is

00:04:27.271 --> 00:04:30.960
unknown, so the demonstration does not invent one.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:37.508
The real Basic reviewer account was checked separately. Both protected tools returned

00:04:37.508 --> 00:04:44.364
PLUS required without protected results. A Basic sign in does not unlock PLUS. The replay

00:04:44.364 --> 00:04:51.220
also verified that revoked test tokens are rejected and normal sign in remains unchanged.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:58.013
For missing inputs, the server rejects invalid calculations. In the actual Claude test, the

00:04:58.013 --> 00:05:05.477
clarified starter prompt asks only miner kind and planning date first, and waits for the answer. The

00:05:05.477 --> 00:05:09.135
initial generic prompt asked for a purchase date,

00:05:09.135 --> 00:05:13.240
which is why our example explicitly says planning date.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:19.392
The actual Claude test refused saved plan loading, GoMining wallet access, buying GOM and

00:05:19.392 --> 00:05:25.820
transfers into locks. Those tools do not exist in this connector. Reviewers can reproduce all

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.138
eight cases with the supplied fictional fixtures

00:05:29.138 --> 00:05:32.940
and dedicated accounts; the applications remain drafts.

